# anytype-llm-wiki — macOS newsyslog.conf(5) reference fragment
#
# newsyslog rotates logs based on size and/or time. This fragment uses a 10 MB
# size trigger, matching the Linux logrotate sample (docs/samples/anytype-llm-wiki.logrotate).
#
# The system-wide /etc/newsyslog.conf is root-only. Two drop-in options:
#
#   (a) Append this fragment to the system config (prompts for sudo):
#         sudo sh -c 'cat docs/samples/anytype-llm-wiki-newsyslog.conf.fragment >> /etc/newsyslog.conf'
#       newsyslog runs daily via launchd (com.apple.newsyslog) and will pick it up.
#
#   (b) Reference it from a per-user launchd wrapper that invokes:
#         newsyslog -F /absolute/path/to/anytype-llm-wiki-newsyslog.conf.fragment
#
# Redirect the server's stderr JSON log to the file with:
#   anytype-llm-wiki serve 2>> ~/Library/Logs/anytype-llm-wiki/run.log
#
# Columns: logfilename [owner:group] mode count size when flags [/pid_file] [sig]
#   mode  600  -> file recreated with rw------- after rotation
#   count 5    -> keep 5 archived generations
#   size  10240 (KB) -> rotate at 10 MB (10240 KB), matching the Linux config
#   when  *    -> size-only trigger (no time-based rotation)
#   flags J    -> compress rotated archives with bzip2 (Z for gzip)
#
# Replace the path and owner below with your own user. newsyslog does NOT expand
# ~; use an absolute path.

/Users/youruser/Library/Logs/anytype-llm-wiki/run.log  youruser:staff  600  5  10240  *  J
